# Commercial deployment

## Safest launch shape

Launch the **Developer** edition first as a single-machine, assisted-install product for private Linux/XAMPP development servers. Keep hub, Agency branding, remote agent selection, and public terminal access out of the offer. Community can be a self-supported acquisition tier.

Before taking payment:

1. place this source in Git and bind the already-reproducible release build to an reviewed commit;
2. disable development licensing and unsigned update acceptance;
3. repeat the clean install, upgrade, failed update, application rollback, and database restore on every advertised OS/XAMPP combination;
4. install and soak-test the rendered worker/health/logrotate assets;
5. run an independent security review focused on terminal, Code Runner, uploads, restores, update extraction, SSRF, and privilege boundaries;
6. publish a support policy, supported-environment matrix, data-handling statement, and recovery runbook;
7. provision a dedicated Safe-mode deployment for any public demo;
8. monitor the first customers with consent and collect diagnostic bundles that exclude secrets.

## Initial limit

The recommended maximum is **5 paid design-partner customers**, each with one MicroSysAdmin machine, assisted onboarding, and a documented rollback path. This is enough to validate environmental variance without creating an unsupported fleet.

Do not sell Studio multi-machine or Agency hub promises as generally available until the real hub, cross-environment installer matrix, signed release service, and multi-organization isolation test suite pass.

## Customer build requirements

- `licensing.development_mode=false`;
- `updates.allow_unsigned_development=false`;
- release channel `stable`;
- Safe profile by default;
- `agent.allow_terminal=false`;
- `webhooks.allow_private_targets=false`;
- hub disabled unless contracted and production-ready;
- HTTPS/private access and no public terminal;
- unique application key and machine/agent credentials;
- external backups of database, storage, config, and `/var/lib/microsysadmin`;
- worker and scheduler supervision;
- log rotation and disk/backup alerts.

## Growth gates

Move above five Developer customers only after two successful update/rollback cycles and a clean-install pass on the supported matrix. Offer Studio only after the real hub and machine allowance reconciliation exist. Offer Agency only after client-group authorization, branding, priority-support operations, tenant isolation, retention controls, and fleet security have external validation.
